🟠 api in shop (prod-eu-1) keeps failing its liveness check (connection refused), so the kubelet keeps restarting it, likely because its containers are not ready when liveness gives up. Liveness gives api 40s (10s delay + 3 × 10s), and api was not ready when each kill came. Its last run lasted 42 seconds; three restarts since its pod was created one hour ago. Fix: give the liveness probe of container app in deployment/api more time (now initialDelaySeconds 10, periodSeconds 10, failureThreshold 3). To read the output of the last crash, run kubectl logs deploy/api -c app -n shop --previous
Proof: both replicas fail, on 2 nodes.
